  "summary": "Ticket EVAL-net-04. Grace Okafor (user_id 11, Receptionist, Admin, America/New_York, usual hours 08:00-16:00) reports she cannot reach the intranet from home; Google works. Checked: account status active, failed_login_count 0, sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true, must_change_password false. Device BL-DT-0111 (Windows 11) online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:58 UTC, no warnings, 70% disk free. Sign-in logs (last 14 days, 10 entries): all successful, no failed_password or mfa_denied, all from New York; VPN sign-ins from residential IP 198.51.100.31 and M365 from corporate IP 203.0.113.10, all during usual hours. Notable: check_mfa_status shows Duo enrollment = false (no method, no device), yet VPN logins are recorded as success with mfa 'none'. KB-013 says VPN requires Duo and to follow KB-004 if not enrolled; KB-004 was not provided and I did not have its content, so I did not enroll anyone. Not yet confirmed whether the user's VPN client is currently connected. Needed: confirm VPN connection state with the user; determine why VPN is accepting logins with no MFA enrollment (possible policy gap); check whether the intranet failure is a VPN routing/DNS issue or a site issue. Not a security block; no red flags of compromise in logs. No actions were queued.",
  "reason": "VPN logins succeed and account is healthy, but the user still cannot reach internal sites, and the account has no Duo enrollment despite VPN access being recorded without MFA. Connection state is unconfirmed and the required KB-004 enrollment guidance is not available to Tier 1, so this needs Tier 2 review."
